9. Real-Time Error Handling and Recovery:
    - Implement a robust error-handling framework that integrates with the system's broader failure recovery strategy, including partial retries and session resumption without compromising data integrity.

10. MD5 Hash Computation Method:
    - Use the standard library function to compute and return the MD5 hash of a given string, handling any exceptions gracefully.

```java
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.math.BigInteger;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;

public static String md5(String str) throws Exception {
    MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
    byte[] bytes = str.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
    digest.update(bytes, 0, bytes.length);
    BigInteger number = new BigInteger(1, digest.digest());
    StringBuilder hashtext = new StringBuilder(number.toString(16));
    while (hashtext.length() < 32) {
        hashtext.insert(0, "0");
    }
    return hashtext.toString();
}
```']

